{"kind":"report","text":"Assessment of the J4 tested-to-landed Source equivalence: SUFFICIENT, with four corrections\n\nI assessed `PROPOSAL.md` (f3c31a7a), `AUDIT.json` (ef04eaf6) and `PINS.json` (1a46386d) in `/private/tmp/artroom-j4-landed-runtime-equivalence-audit-20261031-v1`, for request 87b29d3d. The evidence shows that landed main 112eff12 holds the bytes that Gate 2 tested at 4aa254e9, apart from two documents. The proposed boundary is narrow enough for that one tuple.\n\nThis assessment doesn't adopt the future binding or the operator change. It releases no packet, admission, read or setup.\n\n## What I confirmed\n\n- `git diff --name-status 4aa254e9 112eff12` shows exactly two changed paths, the note and the manifest. Trees 11710061 and 112eff12 are both 32947a56.\n- Outside `notes/` and `*.md`, the modes and blobs at 4aa254e9 and 112eff12 are equal across 2,019 paths. That comparison is my own.\n- `runtime-rows.audit.json` has SHA-256 aa9913fd and 2,019 sorted rows totaling 29,115,800 bytes, and no row is under `notes/` or ends in `.md`. Each row's mode and blob match the tree at 112eff12.\n- Receipt `gate/outer/gate-1/receipt.json` has SHA-256 d581fa94. My review 5830af9b verified the sealed unit.\n- `operator.mjs:54-55` in the V14 packet does compare the gate's head, tree, postHead and postTree with the runtime commit and tree, so it would refuse the real gate at 112eff12. The proposal reads this correctly.\n- The rule in `docs/testing.md`, \"Follow-up after a gate\", says not to rerun the gate for a commit that changes only documents. My review ran `check-notes` and `check-doc-links` at 11710061. So this link is the right tool, and a gate run at main isn't owed.\n\n## Corrections before implementation\n\n1. Base the link on the full-tree comparison. The two-path diff of tracked trees is the proof, and the 2,019-row projection only describes the runtime view. A projection alone wouldn't catch a change to a `.md` file that a runtime path reads. Item 4 of the proposal has the right check, so make it the first check in the validator and refuse if the tracked diff isn't exactly those two paths.\n2. Trace or drop `a0a1d9fd`. The proposal calls it \"the earlier readiness review\" and \"the baseline\". I can't find that prefix as a workroom act or a Git object in this repository. Cite it by its actual ID or path, or don't cite it.\n3. Name the adopting review in the record. \"Record missing approved review\" needs a field to test. The binding should name the checker's review of the operator Source and the exact record digest. This assessment can't fill that field, because neither one exists yet.\n4. Reduce the negatives to the ones that test the boundary. I'd keep three, each with an otherwise valid record: one changed runtime byte, a third documentation path, and a main other than 112eff12. Add one control that restores the old equality and shows the real gate refused. Tampered bindings and altered receipts already fail existing digest checks, so they don't need their own cases.\n\n## Limits\n\n- The equivalence covers 112eff12 only. If the deployment comes from a later main, this record doesn't apply and another review is needed. The proposal says so, and S4 is the likely cause, so the planner should deploy before S4 lands, or expect that review.\n- I didn't read the private state, the V13 predecessor or the V14 custody. I also didn't check the proposal's claims about 21 originals, 14 dispatches or 42 custody files.\n- A clean equivalence proves that the bytes match, and nothing about deployment, the reader or the provider. My two points in 5830af9b still apply to the first live run.\n\n## Architecture\n\nOne closed, digest-pinned record in a separate input fits the operator's existing form, and the historical validators stay untouched. Sufficient.\n\n## Security\n\nThe record can't move: it names one tuple, two paths and one row file, and it allows no latest-main or ancestor rule. With corrections 1 and 3 it holds. No same-source flag can pass.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThree negatives and one control replace the seven in the proposal. The validator adds one branch where the two equalities are today. Sufficient with correction 4.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:59b2eeedf222bd65c56eff7a001423a89b49e99e stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 18 more"}}